  "premise": "Sumire Iwaya, a capable newspaper journalist struggling with depression and anxiety, is dumped by her fiancé and demoted at work. She finds an injured young homeless man outside her building and, half joking, offers to keep him as a pet; he agrees, and she names him Momo after her childhood dog. Their non-sexual but charged cohabitation is tested when her university crush Hasumi, who meets all her stated requirements, re-enters her life. Also known as Tramps Like Us; published in English by Tokyopop and Kodansha USA.",
  "life_message": "A good partner is one who truly understands and comforts you, not one who meets a checklist.",
